/-! # Degree-`3` first-integral `ξ` bridge for the normalized `(8,10)` nonzero source

On the nonzero first face `H = h²`, `N = 5 p₇ H - 4 q₉ = λ h⁹` with
`h.natDegree = 1`, the degree-`5` integral `μ` and the degree-`4`
integral `ν` are cleared and jet-peeled by the imported `ν` integral
bridge; the genuinely unused degree-`3` first integral `ξ` of the same
source differential system is the next isolated mechanism.  Its exact
construction (`xiResidual810`, needing the degree-`5` and degree-`6`
rows a second time), its `d ξ = 0` law on the depressed rows of degree
`8`, `7`, `6`, `5`, `4`, and `3`, its weight-`98` polynomial numerator
(`localClearedFourteenthDefect810 = 8796093022208 h⁹⁸ ξ`), and its
scale-two literal-source power relation
(`nonzeroFace810_fourteenthDefectPowerRelation`, cleared defect
`C xiGround * h₀⁹⁸`) are all reused opaquely from the imported
scale-zero thirteenth-defect scratch — the weight-`84` `μ`, the
weight-`91` `ν`, and the weight-`98` `ξ` numerators are never
re-expanded here, and the spent `μ`/`ν` branch packets are reused as
single opaque propositions.

This file adds the scale-two jet peel and the branch combination.  The
seventeenth-face jet `p₇ = h₀⁶ t₀`, `p₆ = h₀⁴ v₁`, `p₅ = h₀² u₁`,
`q₈ = h₀⁶ s₁`, `q₇ = h₀⁴ w₁`, `q₆ = h₀² b₆₂` factors the `ξ` numerator
through `h₀⁸⁴`, fourteen orders below the defect weight — one order
deeper than the thirteen-order `ν` peel: the peeled power relation is
`head + h₀ · tail = C xiGround · h₀¹⁴`, so the order-`84` head
vanishes at the root of `h₀` on every live branch.  The head is a
`149`-term polynomial in the same eight jet coordinates as the `μ` and
`ν` heads, with every monomial of jet degree at least four.

On the left branch the head reduces, modulo the second/third-defect
reductions, the `Gred`/`Vred` loads, and exact division by the `μ`
left residual — with the first non-monomial quotient of this tower,
`(6/5)(7 t₀² - 8 v₁)` — to a new exact degree-`14` relation on
`(t₀, v₁, u₁, b₆₂)` alone (`bridgeXiLeftResidual810`); the `ν` left
residual does not divide the remainder, and the new relation is not in
the ideal generated by the reduced fourth- through seventh-defect
loads and the `μ` and `ν` left residuals, on either `F₁` or `F₂`, so
it is genuinely new and neither left sub-branch closes.

On the collapsed right branch every jet coordinate is a multiple of
`h₀`, the substituted head and tail acquire four further `h₀` orders —
one deeper than the three-order `ν` collapse — and the quotient peel
collapses to `68719476736` times the ten-term degree-`4` residual
`bridgeXiRightResidual810` on the depth-two jet together with `p₃` and
`q₄`, the first right-branch mechanism to see either: at the root
`16 a₄₁³ s₂ - 50 a₄₁³ v₂ + 30 a₄₁² b₅₁ t₁ - 16 a₄₁² b₄ + 36 a₄₁² b₆₃ v₂
+ 42 a₄₁² w₂ u₂ - 75 a₄₁² u₂² - 40 a₄₁ b₅₁ a₃ + 60 a₄₁ b₅₁ v₂ u₂
+ 36 a₄₁ b₆₃ u₂² + 10 b₅₁ u₂³ = 0`.  Combined with the retained `ν`
alternative `h₀² ∣ p₄ ∨ h₀² ∣ q₅` (whose `p₄` case kills `a₄₁` at the
root and collapses the residual to `10 b₅₁ u₂³ = 0`), this refines to
the strictly deeper alternative
`h₀² ∣ q₅ ∨ (h₀² ∣ p₄ ∧ h₀⁴ ∣ p₅)` on the whole right branch.  The
inhomogeneous Keller boundary relation
`G'(a) W(a) - F(a) X'(a) = j ≠ 0` lives on `p₀, p₁, q₀, q₁`, which
neither new consequence touches, so no branch is genuinely
inconsistent and none is closed.

The `μ` ground constant `eta`, the `ν` ground constant `nuGround`,
the new `ξ` ground constant `xiGround`, the tracked ground constants
`δ, ε, ζ, η`, the aligned face `N = 0`, and both full `μ`/`ν` branch
packets — the left packet with the `F₁ ∨ F₂` alternative, all retained
next-order laws, and both left residuals, and the right packet with
the collapsed zero jet, its divisibility upgrades, both retained
sibling/complementary sub-branches, and the `ν` divisibility
alternative — are preserved and restated opaquely.  The next unused
first integral on this face is the degree-`2` integral
(the next missing input of the scale-zero thirteenth-defect packet).

No total-degree or twice-prime theorem is used.
-/

